James Rising received an email from prospective PhD student Erin Wildes, expressing interest in the School of Marine Science and Policy PhD program and seeking him as an advisor. Erin highlighted her academic background in marine affairs and biology, detailing her research experience related to coastal stressors on oysters and her work with the Mass Oyster Project. James drafted a professional response to inform her that he would not be taking on new students this year while recognizing her qualifications and wishing her well in her search for an advisor.
